# Mobile portrait reader (upright phone)

Willow and all books share one phone reading path: the flipbook iframe with `html.mobile` set by `reader.js` boot script and `reader-runtime.js` `rebuild()`.

## CSS — single source of truth

- **All laid-out restack rules** (cover, title, story, end) live in **one block** in `reader.css`, prefixed with **`html.mobile`**, starting at the comment `Mobile portrait upright reader`.
- **Do not** duplicate the same rules inside `@media (max-width:700px) and (orientation:portrait)` for laid-out pages, cover restack, or story/end flex. Legacy `@media` rules may remain for non–laid-out legacy pages only.
- **Never** set `display:flex` (or `display:grid`) on `.page.laid-out` story pages **without** `.current` on `main > .page`. Hidden pages must stay `display:none` (`html.mobile main>.page:not(.current)`).
- **Never** apply `width:auto` to `.el-image` in the mobile restack; use `.el:not(.el-image)` only. Story art must stay `width:100%` (CSS + `applyMobilePortraitLayout()` in JS).
- Portrait layout JS: skip `fitLaidOut` on mobile; use `applyMobilePortraitLayout()` after rebuild, refit, and flip (`releaseFlip`).

## JS sync

- `reader.js` `bootMobile` and `reader-runtime.js` `rebuild()` must use the **same** portrait matchMedia as each other.
- Do not reintroduce a separate portrait PDF / upright scroll reader for phone; phone = flipbook + `html.mobile` restack.

## Manual regression checklist (Willow, portrait phone)

Before `pp` on reader mobile changes, verify on **Willow’s Big Forest Adventure**:

1. **Open from library** — lands on **cover** (not end, not text soup). Title, tagline, and author readable; no overlapping green story text.
2. **Cover → title → story page 1** — swipe forward; illustration **full width** (not ~half spread width). Text below art, one page of copy visible.
3. **After images finish loading** — illustration **does not shrink** on the current story page.
4. **Mid-book story page** — same full-width art + text; only **one** page visible (no stacked paragraphs from other pages).
5. **Last page (The End)** — character art + “The End” + Read again; no tagline soup.
6. **Read again** — returns to cover cleanly.

If any step fails, fix only the `html.mobile` block or `applyMobilePortraitLayout` / `fitLaidOut` guards — avoid adding a second `@media` mirror.
